      "message": "Thanks!\n\nI suspect this might be muscle memory from Chromium’s `#pragma allow_unsafe_buffers`. That was a custom compiler pragma scoped strictly to the file it appeared in, so it was safe to use in headers. Standard `#pragma clang diagnostic ignored` doesn\u0027t work like that, it changes diagnostic state in the translation unit, so putting it in headers like DrawAtlas.h will silently disable warnings for any code that include one header using it.\n\nCan we move these suppressions into `tools/unsafe_buffers/unsafe_buffers_mappings.txt` instead?\n\ne.g.\n```\n\n[unsafe-buffer-usage]\nsrc:*\n\n# Only enabled in gpu/graphite for now, as a pilot.\n# See http://go/unsafe-buffer-skia\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/*\u003demit\n\n# Temporary exclusions.\n# TODO(564587252): Convert files to SK_UNSAFE_TODO instead of\n# file-wide suppressions.\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/BufferManager.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/ClipAtlasManager.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/ClipStack.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/Context.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/Device.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/DrawAtlas.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/DrawAtlas.h\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/DrawListBase.h\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/GlobalCache.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/GraphicsPipeline.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/ImageFactories.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/Image_YUVA_Graphite.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/KeyHelpers.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/KeyHelpers.h\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/PaintParamsKey.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/PaintParamsKey.h\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/PathAtlas.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/PublicPrecompile.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/Recorder.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/RenderPassDesc.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/RendererProvider.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/RendererProvider.h\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/ResourceCache.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/SerializationUtils.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/ShaderCodeDictionary.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/ShaderInfo.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/SharedContext.cpp\nsrc:*src/gpu/graphite/StorageContext.cpp\nsrc:*src/